Note that I never ascended an arch before, but I frequently see the arc
quest, so this might be worth something.

I love archeologists. The touchstone, sack and pickaxe make them
ressourceful explorers. You can also rely on their speed to run away
from almost everything in the first stages.

The mines are rather tough for them I think, because of the large open
areas it's harder to run away. I tend to wait till they have a good AC
before tackling the mines. Often I'll just do quick visits on the first
level, to try and get a mattock and better armor - a strong pet is
required.

The mattock might be your solution. It's a very good offensive weapon.
It's also easily found in the mines. The pickaxe isn't that bad either
- I rely on it more than on the bullwhip. Run away from anything that
isn't easily killed.

The speed allow you to "dance" around monster. If you time your
movements correctly, You can ensure that they never get a hit on you -
that is for normal and slow speed monsters.

Depending on int and what spellbooks are found, I might switch early to
caster-friendly armor, as archeologists are good casters. Attack,
divination and matter spells are well worth the early practice food
cost. If I find light, force bolt, magic missile, detect food, detect
monsters, I'll seriously consider the caster friendly armor.

A good missile weapon is useful, archs can only get to basic with
dagger, but an enchanted boomerang is very fun to use. It's rather rare
though. Dagger are easily found, and they have a bonus to hit which
makes practice somewhat less painful.
